Quoting  funcrunch  <web-google2@funcrunch.org>:
>I've read that simply picking up tripe and dropping it before your pet
>gets to it is enough to increase apport, as the game keeps track of
>that stat by whether or not the food item was ever in your inventory.

You should be very careful when reading
<http://www.helsinki.fi/~vviitane/spoilers/pets>

For some inexplicable reason it starts with a lot of misinformation and
then reproduces the discussion where that misinformation was debunked.

What you say is - well, slightly confused, because "whether or not the
food item was ever in your inventory" doesn't make a lot of sense in this
context - but while it is true that picking up tripe and dropping it
increases apport, ensuring the pet eats it immediately after the pet drops
an item next to you is best. You don't have to buy it first, so the actual
best plan is to pick up all the tripe and let your pet play in the shop
for a bit.

http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/pets2.html is much more
coherently written but does not discuss gaining apport.
